course: dictionary
lesson: 14938
title: Regulate: control and keep steady
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Regulate is a verb. It means to control something so it stays at the right level or speed, or to control it with rules. Its forms are regulate, regulates, regulated and regulating.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «The thermostat regulates the heat in our house.» A thermostat switches the heating on and off, so regulates must mean controls, keeping the heat at the right level.
explain: «Governments regulate traffic, food and money with laws.» The clue is laws: to regulate can mean to control something with rules. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Governments control traffic with rules" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Science uses regulate too. «Your body regulates its temperature to stay about the same.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Control, or keep steady. Both fit, so that is the meaning.
fact: Regulate means to control something, often to keep it steady or within rules.
fact: «Regulate temperature» means keeping the temperature at the right level.
fact: «Strictly regulated» means controlled by very firm rules.
fact: «Regulate the flow» means controlling how much moves through, or how fast it goes.
fact: Your body regulates its temperature by sweating when you are hot and shivering when you are cold.
exercise: «The thermostat regulates the heat in the house.» What does regulates mean here? | Turns the lights off every night | Makes the heat go higher and higher | Stops people from ever feeling warm | *Controls the heat to keep it at the right level
exercise: «Your body regulates its temperature to stay about the same.» How does the body do this? | *By sweating when hot and shivering when cold | By eating lots of sweets | By growing taller each day | By sleeping for a whole week
exercise: «Governments regulate traffic with laws.» Which word has the closest meaning to regulate? | Celebrate | Ignore | *Control | Hide
test: «The shop's food is strictly regulated by the council.» What does strictly regulated suggest? | Given away for free to everyone | Forgotten by all the shops | *Controlled by very firm rules | Sold only on Sundays
test: Which sentence uses regulate correctly? | The sun regulates a loud song. | *The tap regulates the flow of water. | The tree regulates its sadness.
exam: Sam says regulate means to break the rules. Which is correct? | *Regulate means to control something, often with rules, and not to break them | Regulate means to be very loud | Regulate means to break things on purpose | Regulate means to fall asleep quickly
